<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Shurp | Privacy Policy</title>

    <link href="../assets/css/style.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
</head>

<body class="bg-[#E6F1F7] text-[#1F2933] font-['Inter'] px-4">

    <nav class="nav-bar">
        <div class="flex items-center">
            <a href="./">
                <img src="../assets/logo.png" alt="Shurp" class="h-8 md:h-10 w-auto">
            </a>
        </div>
        <a href="./" class="text-sm font-medium text-white/70 hover:text-white transition">← Back</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="legal-card">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tighter mb-2">Privacy Policy: Shurp</h1>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-40 mb-10 italic">Last updated: May 2026</p>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <h2 class="!border-l-0 !pl-0 !mb-4 text-xl">1. Our Philosophy: Less is Safer.</h2>
                <p class="!mb-4 !opacity-100">We do not collect data we do not need, and we do not store it longer than
                    necessary.</p>
                <p class="!mb-0 !opacity-100">Your privacy is built into our app architecture.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>2. Who is the Data Controller?</h2>
            <p>Your personal data controller is SIA Shurp, Reg. No. LV40203709369, Email for privacy inquiries: <span
                    id="safe-email-p2"></span></p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>3. What Data Do We Process?</h2>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Public profile (visible to all users):</strong> Name, profile photo, "About me" text
                    description, ride preferences (music, smoking, etc.), vehicle make and model (drivers only),
                    verification status, and "Supporter" badge. Profile photos are stored in Supabase Storage (Ireland,
                    EU) with a public URL so other users can see them on profiles and in ride results.</li>
                <li><strong>Reviews.</strong> After a ride you may leave a rating (1–5 stars) and a comment about
                    another
                    participant. These ratings are publicly visible on the other user's profile together with your name
                    and profile photo. Ratings remain available even after you delete your account, but they are
                    anonymized.</li>
                <li><strong>Private data (visible only to you):</strong> Your email address is used for authentication
                    and communication (for example, password reset). Your password is stored in encrypted form and is
                    not
                    visible to anyone, including Shurp administration.</li>
                <li><strong>Data for confirmed ride participants (disclosed only after the ride is
                        confirmed):</strong> Full name and phone number. The phone number is disclosed securely in the
                    app so ride participants can contact each other. After the ride, this data is not publicly
                    available.</li>
                <li><strong>Location data:</strong> The app processes only the start points, destinations, and routes
                    you
                    specify yourself. There is no background tracking. If you use your device's location, that
                    information
                    is used only to determine a specific address. If you create a ride alert, your searched route
                    (start–destination) is stored until you delete it or turn it off.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> Device IP address, operating system version, and error reports —
                    for
                    system maintenance.</li>
                <li><strong>Notification data:</strong> Your device's unique notification identifier (FCM token) —
                    required to send push notifications. It is deleted when you delete your account.</li>
                <li><strong>Help section:</strong> If you contact support, we store your request, email, and technical
                    information (for example, device type) so we can respond.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>4. Verification Data (Identity Confirmation)</h2>
            <p>To promote safety and mutual trust in the community, Shurp offers identity verification using an
                independent service provider based in the European Union, Didit (Didit Solutions S.L.).</p>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Standards compliance:</strong> Didit is a GDPR-compliant platform registered in the European
                    Union that provides digital processing of identity documents in line with the core principles of the
                    eIDAS regulation.</li>
                <li><strong>Verification process:</strong> For drivers: driver's licence check to obtain verified
                    status.
                    For passengers: voluntary identity document check (ID card or passport).</li>
                <li><strong>How we process this data:</strong> Document scanning, data reading, and biometric comparison
                    take place in Didit's secure environment. Only the final result is stored in Shurp's database:
                    "Verified: Yes/No" and a unique encrypted identifier.</li>
                <li><strong>Data storage and access:</strong> We do not store document images, serial numbers, or
                    personal
                    identification numbers on our servers. Shurp administration accesses Didit data only in exceptional
                    cases: investigating security incidents, resolving legal disputes, fixing errors, or at your direct
                    request.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>5. Communication Between Users.</h2>
            <p>After a ride is confirmed, participants can communicate in two ways:</p>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Shurp in-app chat</strong> — message content is stored on our servers (Supabase, EU) for up
                    to 90 days after the ride for safety and dispute resolution. After that, content is deleted, but
                    metadata (who, when, and with whom you communicated) is kept for 1 more year.</li>
                <li><strong>WhatsApp handoff</strong> — at the user's own choice. In that case, communication takes
                    place
                    on Meta's servers in accordance with WhatsApp's privacy policy, and Shurp is not involved.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>6. Data Security.</h2>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Access restriction:</strong> Access to user verification data on the third-party platform
                    (Didit) is limited to authorized Shurp administrators only.</li>
                <li><strong>Data segregation:</strong> Your public profile never displays private data — only the fact
                    of
                    verification.</li>
                <li><strong>Encryption:</strong> All communication between Shurp, Didit, and your device is encrypted
                    (TLS/SSL).</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>7. Legal Basis for Data Processing</h2>
            <p>Data processing is based on:</p>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Contract performance:</strong> To provide the service and connect you with other users.</li>
                <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> Ensuring security, preventing fraud, and improving the
                    service.</li>
                <li><strong>Consent:</strong> When you grant access to device features (for example, camera or
                    location).
                </li>
                <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> Ride data (route, price, date) is stored for 5 years in
                    accordance
                    with Latvian tax and transport law requirements. Data is linked to an anonymous user identifier —
                    not
                    your name or contact information. When you delete your account, this identifier is also permanently
                    removed.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>8. How Long Do We Store Data?</h2>
            <p>We do not store data longer than necessary for the purpose for which it was collected:</p>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Active rides:</strong> stored for up to 10 days after the ride, then moved to the archive.
                </li>
                <li><strong>Ride archive:</strong> stored for 5 years in accordance with legal requirements, then
                    automatically deleted.</li>
                <li><strong>Chat content:</strong> deleted 90 days after the ride. Technical metadata (who messaged whom
                    and when) — after 1 year.</li>
                <li><strong>User complaints:</strong> anonymized after they expire, retaining only statistical data.
                </li>
                <li><strong>When you delete your account:</strong> all personal data is permanently deleted. Only
                    anonymous ride data remains in the ride archive, with no link to your identity.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>9. Data Sharing and Security</h2>
            <p>We do not sell data to third parties and never pass your personal data to advertisers.</p>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Advertising:</strong> Shurp does not currently show ads in the app. If advertising is
                    introduced in the future, we will update this policy and ask for your consent before showing ads in
                    accordance with GDPR and the ePrivacy rules (for example, iOS App Tracking Transparency and consent
                    dialogs in Europe).</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Data may be shared only with:</p>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Ride participants</strong> - name and phone number only after the ride is confirmed.
                    Communication primarily takes place in Shurp's in-app chat; at the user's choice it may continue in
                    the WhatsApp app (Meta Platforms Ireland Limited), which is subject to WhatsApp's privacy policy.
                </li>
                <li><strong>Technical partners:</strong> Supabase Inc. (server infrastructure, authentication, database
                    and file storage, hosted in Ireland, EU); Didit Solutions S.L. (Spain, EU — identity verification);
                    Google Ireland Limited (push notifications via Firebase Cloud Messaging); Apple Inc. / Google LLC
                    (if
                    you sign in with Apple ID or a Google account, partners provide us with your email address and, for
                    Google, your name and a link to your profile photo stored on Google's servers. Apple App Store /
                    Google Play (for voluntary "Supporter" payments — Shurp does not receive or store payment card
                    data).</li>
            </ul>
            <p>All technical partners operate under Data Processing Agreements (DPA) and GDPR.</p>
            <p>All data is encrypted both in transit (TLS) and at rest.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>10. Your Rights (GDPR)</h2>
            <p>Under GDPR, you have the following rights:</p>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>Access:</strong> request at any time what data we hold about you.</li>
                <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
                <li><strong>Erasure:</strong> request deletion of your data when it is no longer necessary.</li>
                <li><strong>Restriction:</strong> request restriction of data processing.</li>
                <li><strong>Data portability:</strong> request a copy of your data for download or transfer to another
                    service.</li>
                <li><strong>Objection:</strong> object to processing based on legitimate interests.</li>
                <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent:</strong> withdraw previously given consent at any time.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Send requests to <span id="safe-email-p10"></span>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>
            <p>If you believe your data is being processed unlawfully, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the
                Data State Inspectorate (<a href="https://www.dvi.gov.lv"
                    class="text-[#125E8A] hover:underline font-semibold" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">www.dvi.gov.lv</a>).</p>
        </section>

        <div class="pt-8 text-center">
            <a href="./"
                class="text-[#125E8A] font-bold hover:opacity-80 transition underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Back
                to Homepage</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="py-12 px-8 bg-[#125E8A] text-center text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest">
        <p class="text-white/70">&copy; 2026 SHURP. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>

