            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.3.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Tax treatment:</strong> No personal income tax refund or other tax
                    reliefs applicable to gifts or donations apply to the Support Payment.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.3.5.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Effect on use:</strong> This payment is not consideration for a
                    specific trip and does not give the user any priority in trip reservations or other Platform
                    features.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Advertising and Freemium:</strong> Shurp reserves the right to
                    display advertising content on the Platform. Users may be offered a paid subscription option
                    (hereinafter – "Freemium").</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.4.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Service content:</strong> A "Freemium" subscription gives the User
                    the technical ability to use the Platform without displaying third-party advertising content.</span>
            </p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.4.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Functional separation:</strong> The Freemium fee is payment for
                    digital content (removal of advertising), not for a transport service. Purchasing a subscription
                    does not in any way affect trip availability, does not increase the likelihood of reservation
                    confirmation, and does not impose on Shurp responsibility for users' mutual performance of
                    agreements.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.4.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Subscription process:</strong> Freemium payments are processed
                    through app store (Apple App Store or Google Play Store) subscription systems. Cancellation of a
                    subscription and refund requests are handled in accordance with the rules of the relevant app
                    store.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.4.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Pricing policy:</strong> Information on Freemium price and
                    subscription period (for example, monthly or annual) is published on the Platform before purchase.
                    Shurp reserves the right to unilaterally change the subscription price, notifying existing
                    subscribers in the manner prescribed by the app store.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.5.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Tax disclaimer:</strong> When making a support payment or
                    subscribing to services, the transaction is between the User and SIA Shurp. Cost-sharing for trips
                    is a private transaction between the Driver and Passenger in which Shurp is not involved and for
                    which it bears no responsibility.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.6.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Nature of the service:</strong> Shurp is an information society
                    service (the Platform) that provides a technical environment for communication between natural
                    persons. Shurp is not a transport service provider, carrier, or taxi service operator under
                    applicable local law. The Platform does not manage vehicles, issue work orders, employ drivers, or
                    set commercial fares. All trips are private agreements between Users aimed at sharing trip costs,
                    not making a profit.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.7.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Contractual relations:</strong> By using the Platform, the Driver
                    and Passenger enter into a mutual agreement regarding the trip. Shurp is not a party to this
                    agreement, is not its guarantor, and does not assume responsibility for its performance. This
                    agreement is characterized as a private law transaction between two natural persons.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.8.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Nature of ride-sharing and prohibition of profit</strong></span>
            </p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.8.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Nature of ride-sharing:</strong> Trips published on the Shurp
                    platform are trips the Driver already planned to make for their own personal needs regardless of
                    whether a Passenger joins. A Passenger's presence does not change the trip's purpose or destination.
                    Ride-sharing available on the Platform is a non-commercial, social activity aimed at sharing travel
                    costs, not making a profit. Shurp provides an automated tool for calculating the maximum permissible
                    costs to help Users comply with fair cost-sharing principles.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.8.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Prohibition of profit:</strong> The Driver represents and warrants
                    that the total amount received from Passengers does not exceed the direct and variable operating
                    costs of the vehicle (fuel, taxes, insurance, and depreciation) on the specific route.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.8.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>User responsibility:</strong> Any profit-making through the
                    Platform is strictly prohibited and is considered an individual User breach. The Driver assumes full
                    responsibility for the compliance of their activities with local tax and commercial activity laws
                    (including in relation to revenue authorities or tax administration bodies).</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">1.9.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Role of the Platform and technical infrastructure:</strong>
                    Shurp's role is limited to providing an information society service, which includes technical
                    infrastructure for communication, user profile management, and informative cost-sharing calculation.
                    Shurp is not involved in users' mutual payments, does not guarantee that trips take place, and does
                    not assume responsibility for users' mutual performance of agreements.</span></p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>2. Participant Registration and Requirements</h2>

            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>General rules and registration:</strong></span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.1.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Age restriction:</strong> Platform services are available to
                    natural persons who have reached at least 18 (eighteen) years of age. By registering on the
                    Platform, the User confirms that they are of legal age. Shurp reserves the right to request proof of
                    age (for example, through identity verification) and to delete the account without delay if it is
                    established that the User has not reached 18 years of age. Any data concerning minors, if
                    identified, is deleted in accordance with GDPR Article 17.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.1.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Account creation and verification:</strong> A User account is
                    created using an email address or integrated social network accounts (for example, Apple, Google).
                    Shurp reserves the right to request additional proof of identity before use of certain features (for
                    example, creating a trip offer), and to request additional information or proof of identity if
                    doubts arise regarding the truthfulness of the account or compliance with these terms.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.1.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Identity and one account:</strong> The User undertakes to provide
                    truthful information (real first and last name) and to use only one personal account. Concealing
                    identity, creating pseudonyms or fake profiles, or transferring an account to third parties is
                    strictly prohibited.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Driver requirements and verification:</strong> When creating a
                    trip offer, the Driver represents and legally warrants that:</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.2.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body">They hold a valid driving licence of the appropriate category recognized
                    in the country where the trip takes place.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.2.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body">The vehicle has a valid national technical inspection and mandatory civil
                    liability insurance (for example, OCTA in Latvia or its lawful equivalent in other EU
                    countries).</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.2.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body">The vehicle is in a technical condition that complies with local road
                    traffic rules and does not endanger road safety.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.2.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Driver data verification:</strong> To enhance community safety,
                    Shurp verifies identity and driving licence data using the third-party service provider Didit ID
                    Verify (hereinafter – the Processor), which acts as a data processor within the meaning of GDPR
                    Article 28 on behalf of SIA Shurp. Shurp does not store the User's personal identification number,
                    document numbers, or images thereof – only an encrypted verification status (approved/rejected) is
                    maintained. Detailed information on the Processor's activities is available in the <a
                        href="privacy.html" class="text-[#125E8A] hover:underline font-semibold">Privacy
                        Policy</a>.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Passenger duties and safety:</strong></span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.3.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Personal booking:</strong> A trip must be booked in your own name.
                    Booking on behalf of third parties is permitted only with prior, clear agreement with the Driver
                    through the Platform's communication tools. You may not book a seat for minors without an
                    accompanying person.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.3.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Minors and safety:</strong> It is prohibited to book a seat for
                    minors without an accompanying adult.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.3.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Transport of children:</strong> Transporting children requires
                    appropriate special equipment (child seat or booster) in accordance with the laws of the country
                    where the trip takes place.</span></p>
            <ul class="compact-list compact-list--nested">
                <li>The Passenger has a duty, before confirming the trip, to inform the Driver about travelling with a
                    minor and to provide an appropriate child seat unless the Driver has clearly indicated on the
                    platform that a child seat is available in the vehicle.</li>
                <li>The Driver has the right and duty to refuse the trip if safety requirements are not met. In such a
                    case the Driver is not liable for consequences arising from the refusal.</li>
                <li>The Passenger undertakes to arrive at the agreed time and not to distract the Driver while driving
                    the vehicle.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">2.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body">Account suspension. Shurp reserves the right at any time without notice to
                    suspend or delete a User account, or to restrict access to the Platform, if these terms, local
                    regulations, or the safety of other users are breached.</span></p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>3. Cost-Sharing Principle and Payments</h2>
            <p>Shurp is based on fair, non-commercial cost-sharing among fellow travellers.</p>

            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">3.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Separation of payments and disclaimer of
                        liability.</strong></span></p>
            <p>Users confirm that they distinguish two types of financial relationship on the platform:</p>
            <ul class="compact-list">
                <li><strong>▪︎ Platform payments:</strong> Payments for a Freemium subscription or voluntary support are
                    made through app stores (Apple App Store / Google Play Store) and constitute a direct contractual
                    relationship between the User and SIA Shurp.</li>
                <li><strong>▪︎ Ride-sharing expenses:</strong> Payments to cover trip costs are a private transaction
                    between the Driver and Passenger. Shurp does not process these payments, does not maintain user
                    financial accounts for trip payment, and does not charge a commission. Shurp is not liable for
                    payment delays, refusals, or disputes relating to cost-sharing for trips, and Users are themselves
                    responsible for fulfilling their tax obligations.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">3.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Non-commercial nature:</strong> In accordance with the Republic of
                    Latvia and general European Union carpooling principles, the Driver may not profit from a trip. A
                    Passenger's contribution covers only a proportional share of the trip's direct costs (fuel, road
                    tolls, parking) and variable operating costs (vehicle wear and tear). For a trip to be classified as
                    non-commercial cost-sharing, the total amount received from all Passengers must at no time exceed
                    the total operating costs of the specific route. The Driver may not retain a financial surplus
                    (profit) from the trip.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">3.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Algorithm control:</strong> To prevent the possibility of
                    profit-making, the Platform's algorithm automatically calculates and sets the maximum cost-sharing
                    amount for each trip. The Driver may not request from Passengers an amount exceeding this
                    platform-set limit.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">3.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Private settlements:</strong> Users independently agree among
                    themselves on the method and timing of payment (for example, cash or private bank transfer).</span>
            </p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">3.5.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Cost-sharing record and tax compliance.</strong></span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">3.5.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body">To protect Users in the event of possible tax authority audits (for
                    example, the Latvian State Revenue Service or the tax authorities of the relevant country), Shurp
                    automatically retains a record of each trip for 5 (five) years. The record includes the route, the
                    maximum operating costs calculated by the Platform in accordance with fair cost-sharing principles,
                    the amount actually agreed, and the date.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">3.5.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body">This record serves as technical evidence that the specific trip qualifies
                    as non-commercial cost-sharing (carpooling), not economic activity or a transport service. This
                    record is available to the relevant User upon reasonable request by writing to <span
                        id="safe-email-352"></span>. Users themselves assume full responsibility for complying with
                    local tax and other financial obligations towards the authorities of their country of
                    residence.</span></p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>4. Safety and Liability</h2>

            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Insurance and legal basis:</strong> The Driver confirms that they
                    have valid compulsory civil liability insurance for the vehicle owner (in Latvia – OCTA, in other
                    countries – equivalent MTPL insurance) in force for the entire trip route. In accordance with EU
                    directives and local regulations, compulsory civil liability insurance covers losses to Passengers
                    (third parties) where the trip is non-commercial (cost-sharing). The Driver is fully responsible for
                    compliance with the terms of their insurance policy.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Identity verification:</strong> To ensure safety, Users have the
                    right before the trip begins to ask the other party to present an identity document or driving
                    licence to verify that identity matches the profile indicated on the Platform. Parties have the
                    right to refuse a trip to a person whose identity does not match the booking.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>User conduct, safety, and environment</strong></span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.3.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Responsibility for conduct:</strong> Users are themselves fully
                    responsible for their behaviour, personal safety, and belongings. Shurp provides only a platform for
                    communication and does not assume liability for events during a trip.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.3.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Respectful environment and zero tolerance:</strong> The Shurp
                    Platform is founded on mutual respect and safety. Any form of disrespectful, offensive, or
                    aggressive behaviour is prohibited on the Platform. This includes, but is not limited to, unwanted
                    communication, any form of harassment, or physical and verbal abuse. Users undertake to observe
                    generally accepted standards of courtesy and to respect other users' privacy both during and after a
                    trip.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.3.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Belongings:</strong> Shurp is not liable for items lost, damaged,
                    or left in the vehicle. Users are advised to check their personal belongings before getting
                    out.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Emergency situations and reporting</strong></span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.4.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Shurp is not an emergency service:</strong> The Shurp Platform is
                    not considered an emergency or safety service. Shurp does not provide immediate real-time response
                    to incidents.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.4.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Action in critical situations:</strong> In any situation that
                    threatens health, life, or safety (for example, a road traffic accident, aggression, or a medical
                    problem), the User has a duty to contact immediately on their own the operational services of the
                    relevant country (for example, by calling the European unified emergency number 112).</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.4.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body">Platform notification after an incident. Only after the immediate threat
                    has been removed and law enforcement authorities have been informed is the User invited to inform
                    the Platform of what occurred using the "Report" function (see section 6.3). Based on the report
                    received, Shurp may take measures to restrict or delete the relevant User's account.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.5.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Limitation of liability (Exclusion of Liability):</strong></span>
            </p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.5.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>"As is":</strong> The Platform is provided "as is" and "as
                    available". Shurp does not guarantee uninterrupted operation or the absolute accuracy of information
                    provided by Users.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.5.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Accidents and disputes:</strong> Shurp is only an information
                    intermediary and is not liable for road traffic accidents, bodily injury, material loss, trip delay
                    or cancellation, or any mutual disputes between Users.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">4.5.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Financial cap:</strong> As Shurp does not charge for use of the
                    Platform's core features, insofar as permitted by applicable law, Shurp's aggregate liability to the
                    User in respect of any claim is limited to EUR 0 (zero euros). This limitation does not apply where
                    liability arises from Shurp's gross negligence, wilful misconduct, or where mandatory consumer
                    protection rules provide otherwise.</span></p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>5. Account Restriction, Suspension, and Deletion</h2>

            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Platform rights:</strong> Shurp reserves the right at its
                    discretion and without prior notice to restrict access to the Platform, suspend, or permanently
                    delete a User account in the following cases:</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.1.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Breach of terms:</strong> If these Terms of Use or Platform
                    community standards are breached.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.1.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Breach of law:</strong> If the User's actions contravene
                    applicable regulations or there are reasonable grounds to suspect unlawful commercial activity or
                    fraud.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.1.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Safety and trust risks:</strong> If there are reasonable grounds
                    to suspect creation of a fake profile, provision of false information, or conduct that may harm the
                    Platform and its users' safety.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.1.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Systematic complaints and reputation:</strong> If repeated
                    substantiated complaints are received about the User from other carpoolers or if the User's overall
                    reputation on the Platform indicates systematic non-compliance with these Terms or generally
                    accepted standards of conduct.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.1.5.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Signs of commercial activity:</strong> If the User's activity (for
                    example, an unreasonably large number of trips or attempts to manipulate costs) indicates an aim to
                    profit rather than to share costs.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.1.6.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Inactivity:</strong> If the account has not been used for a
                    prolonged period (more than 24 months).</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body">Notice of decision and appeal. In the event of restriction, suspension, or
                    deletion of an account, Shurp informs the User by sending a notice to the registered email address
                    or using in-app notifications. The notice states the grounds for the decision (within the meaning of
                    DSA Article 17), except where providing such information is restricted for security reasons to
                    protect other persons' privacy or to comply with legal requirements. The User has the right to
                    challenge the decision within 14 (fourteen) days of receiving the notice by sending a written
                    submission to <span id="safe-email-52"></span>.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Consequences and restrictions.</strong></span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.3.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Cancellation of reservations:</strong> In the event of account
                    suspension or deletion, all existing and pending reservations are automatically cancelled. Shurp is
                    not liable for loss or inconvenience (for example, the need to find alternative transport) resulting
                    from such cancellation.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.3.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Financial obligations:</strong> Deletion of an account does not
                    release the User from the obligation to settle private financial obligations towards other Users
                    that arose before the account was closed.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.3.3.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Prohibition of re-registration:</strong> A User whose account has
                    been deleted for breach of these Terms is strictly prohibited from creating a new profile using
                    other data or identity. Shurp reserves the right to use technical identifiers to block repeated
                    registration attempts.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">5.3.4.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Data retention for security:</strong> Shurp reserves the right to
                    retain necessary User data after account deletion (for example, phone number or device ID) insofar
                    as necessary for security purposes and to prevent re-registration, in accordance with the Privacy
                    Policy and GDPR exceptions.</span></p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>6. Shurp Community Guidelines.</h2>
            <p>For ride-sharing to be pleasant and safe for everyone, Users undertake to observe the following
                principles:</p>

            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">6.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Accuracy and communication:</strong></span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">6.1.1.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>Keeping others informed:</strong> If plans change or there is a
                    delay, it is your duty to inform the other party without delay using the Platform's communication
                    tools.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-2"><span class="legal-clause-num">6.1.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>No-show ("Ghosting"):</strong> Repeated failure to appear for a
                    trip without prior notice is considered a material breach of these Terms and may result in immediate
                    restriction of access to the Platform.</span></p>
            <p class="legal-clause legal-clause--depth-1"><span class="legal-clause-num">6.2.</span> <span
                    class="legal-clause-body"><strong>House rules during a trip:</strong></span></p>
